== Primary documentary source and scope ==
[[Media:Decipher_Glossary_1998.pdf|November 1998, Glossary Version 2.0]], page 82.
The actual 1998 preface (page 2) distinguishes most clarifying revisions from 17 gray Errata gameplay changes. Let page 82 is normal type, not a marked gray gameplay erratum; compared with the printed face, its first function spells out the globally defined equivalent "dejarik battle" (Glossary page 47). The 2002 preface (page 1) replaces same-name entries unless "See Glossary"; Let page 5 publishes the Play-on/present-with wording and is not marked as a new change in that update. These source-wording publications are preserved without manufacturing an Errata ordinal, executable state or physical printing.

The source excerpt is rendered from the actual composed page rectangle <code>[180, 489, 503, 590]</code> at 745/rectangle-width. Its image includes the following clarification paragraph; game_text contains only the published wording block, not that commentary. The 1998 complete PDF SHA-256 is <code>9af0cafcd4bb8b921f5e587c8472174001319415aa4d1a3ca9a08a525ee1cfc7</code>; the 2002 complete PDF SHA-256 is <code>1b1bad05cae4484a4fafae6b7ecc21e2f7697899e10a38c0f85f31f47db90c39</code>. Metadata is source-qualified: explicitly inherited verified-host uniqueness, no executable identifier, no conditional character values. Printed edition/update dates are not claimed as original first-publication days of reused wording.